# ==============================================================================
# RAG Intelligence System
# Source: EXECUTION.md section 9 "Files that must be ignored" (verbatim block),
# plus platform additions marked below.
#
# RULE - instruction 6 in section 0 of RAG-INTELLIGENCE-POC-EXECUTION.md, verbatim:
#   "Never put client PDFs, extracted text, SQLite files, vectors, generated
#    reports, secrets, user data, prompts or answers in Git, GitHub Actions
#    artifacts, logs, screenshots or issue bodies."
# Section 3.1 of the same file extends it to document filenames and hashes.
# (This header previously cited "section 6" with a paraphrase; section 6 of that
# file is governed learning. Corrected 2026-09-21.)
# ==============================================================================

# --- section 9 verbatim ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
backend/data/
backend/models/
uploads/
*.pdf
*.sqlite*
*.lance/
*.onnx
*.gguf
ollama-models/
node_modules/
dist/
.venv/
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
playwright-report/
test-results/

# --- additions (not in section 9; required for this environment) ---
# Synthetic CI fixtures are the ONLY PDFs allowed in Git. Re-include explicitly.
!tests/fixtures/synthetic/*.pdf

# Scratch folders left by audit runs (pytest basetemp and similar). Ignored
# explicitly because their subfolders can be permission-denied, which makes git
# unable to see them at all - invisible is not the same as ignored, and a later
# `git add -A` run with different permissions would sweep them in.
.audit_tmp*/

# Project memory (.cowork): DEFAULT-DENY. Most of it is evidence - client
# document names and hashes, prompts, model answers, DB row ids - which rule 6
# above keeps out of Git; it travels by direct copy. Only policy and plan files
# are allowed, each named here. A new .cowork file is therefore ignored until
# someone decides it is safe, instead of committed until someone notices.
# Transport of each file: .cowork/README-INDEX.md.
.cowork/*
!.cowork/NORTH-STAR.md
!.cowork/README-INDEX.md
!.cowork/CLIENT_FEEDBACK_REQUIREMENTS_ADDENDUM.md
!.cowork/EXECUTE-B24-B23.md
!.cowork/EXECUTE-COMMIT-B24-B23.md
!.cowork/EXECUTE-GITHUB-TRANSFER.md
!.cowork/EXECUTE-RAM-OPTIMISATION.md
!.cowork/LAPTOP-MODEL-UPGRADE-9B.md
!.cowork/RAM-OPTIMISATION.md
# Tracked since 44f66ec, before this rule; carries no document identifier.
!.cowork/PROMPT-crs-client-fields.md

# Windows / macOS noise
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# Editors
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# Python build/coverage
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
.coverage
htmlcov/
coverage.xml

# Node / Vite
.vite/
vite.config.*.timestamp-*
npm-debug.log*
*.tsbuildinfo

# Local runtime artifacts (defence in depth - these must never be committed)
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.duckdb
backend/storage/
logs/
*.log
benchmarks/local/

# Secret-scanning tool output
gitleaks-report.json

# Generated codebase snapshots. Valuable to read, but "as of the current
# commit" goes stale silently - the same defect class as a field that
# certifies state it never read. Regenerate rather than track.
Claude outputs/

# Claude Code per-machine permissions (never shared)
.claude/settings.local.json

# Filled gold sheets describe client standards - template only (gold/README.md)
gold/*.csv
!gold/TEMPLATE.csv
